{-# OPTIONS --rewriting --local-confluence-check #-}

-- Martin-Löf type theory on the same machinery, as a test of whether the
-- construction carries over to a dependently typed object language.
--
-- ONE syntactic sort: types are terms.  The signature is Pi, lam, app, a
-- universe, and Nat with a natrec whose successor branch binds TWO
-- variables at once.  agdasubst.py accepted it unchanged and emitted the
-- 90 rules below, so single-sortedness is the degenerate case of the
-- multi-sorted setting rather than a separate one.
--
-- Typing is extrinsic (Curry/PTS), definitional equality of types is
-- untyped conversion, and the universe is Type : Type.  The last is
-- logically inconsistent by Girard's paradox and type-safe regardless,
-- because neither preservation nor progress needs normalization.  It is
-- chosen so the universe costs nothing that would distract from the
-- measurement.
--
-- THE MEASUREMENT: subject reduction and progress are proved with ZERO
-- substitution lemmas applied by hand, the same count as systemf.agda.
-- That includes the two cases System F has no analogue of, the motive
-- commuting with a double lift and the two-variable simultaneous
-- ι-substitution of the natrec successor branch.
--
-- What MLTT adds is not substitution work but judgment plumbing:
-- stability of reduction and conversion under substitution (19 cases),
-- context conversion (13), and inversion through the conversion rule.
-- In MLTT, Π-injectivity is needed for SUBJECT REDUCTION itself, not
-- only for progress, because a lambda may reach its Π-type by
-- conversion.
--
-- ONE assumption, fun-ext, function extensionality, which the generated
-- core's function model needs and which is conservative over Agda's
-- theory.  mltt-vec.agda drops even that.  Church-Rosser for the untyped
-- β/ι calculus is PROVED below by Takahashi's method, and Π-injectivity
-- and no-confusion follow from it.
-- No holes.  No TERMINATING pragmas.
--
-- The positive controls are at the end: the confluence checker and the
-- refl-probes are demonstrably able to report failure.

